  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<b>Your job</b>

    Users send a ticket when their PC has a problem.
    Fix every PC before too many users are lost.


    <b>Connecting</b>

    Click
    a ticket in the list to connect to that PC. Connecting takes a few seconds, and
    you can only work on one PC at a time. Disconnect with the button above the list.
    When you fix a PC, its session closes by itself.


    <b>The list goes stale</b>

    While
    you are connected, the other tickets stop updating: they are dimmed and show
    how they were when you last switched. When a PC you can''t see takes damage,
    you hear a beep and its ticket flashes red.


    <b>Pressure and damage</b>

    Every
    PC has a pressure meter that fills while its problem is unsolved, also while
    you are working on another PC. When it is full, the PC takes damage: Fine, Slightly
    broken, More broken, Blackout. At Blackout the user is lost.


    <b>How each
    PC is fixed</b>

    The ''i'' button on the remote PC explains the minigame
    of the PC you are connected to.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
